What follows is the record as received, presented so the maintainer can verify it against the main line:

1. **Overload selection by full signature (`List.remove`)** — the symptom was three separate infinite loops, all one shape: Java calling `list.remove(int)` (delete by index) while the engine ran `remove(Object)` (or vice versa), because dispatch was by argument count, not type. `remove(int)` confused with `remove(Object)` means searching for a numeric object never present → removal never happens → loop condition never turns false → **infinite loop**. The fix: overload selection on the full signature (arity + argument types). With it, all three loops died simultaneously.
2. **Real `Environment`/`StatFs` values** — environmental NPEs on the storage-preparation path (empty shadows answering `getExternalStorageDirectory()`/`StatFs`); fixed by answering real path and filesystem-stat values as AOSP does.
3. **Real battery values** — `BatteryManager` always answering 0% made Telegram permanently raise the low-battery warning banner; fixed by answering real status/percentage/charge state. *(Observable consequence in a pre-fix build: `LowPowerEnabledTitle` present in the tree — exactly what my tree shows today.)*
4. **The AndroidUtilities bypass** — the biggest change: Telegram's `org.telegram.messenger.AndroidUtilities` toolbox (~460 methods) was partially shadowed; every incomplete point meant a subtle UI wrong-turn. The fix pulled the class **out of the shadow path so the real DEX executes itself** — the project's core orientation: wherever the DEX can execute, let it execute; shadows only for genuinely native system APIs.
5. **`View.animate` without NPE** — `View.animate()` returning `null` → NPE at main-screen construction; fixed by materializing the `ViewPropertyAnimator` shadow with AOSP's fluent self-returning behavior. *(For orientation: my tree already carries the per-view cached `ViewPropertyAnimator` infrastructure at `miniandroid/src/framework/android_shadows.cpp:3396` from an earlier session — the wave-3 change was on top of that line.)*

